 "notes": [
  "The suggested catalogue match (Adafruit HT16K33 FeatherWing) is wrong for this tutorial; the plain 8x8 LED matrix (led-matrix-8x8, 1088AS-style, ports R1-R8 / C1-C8) was used instead.",
  "Pin mapping follows the manual's table: matrix pin 1 (row5)=13, 2 (row7)=12, 3 (col2)=11, 4 (col3)=10, 5 (row8)=A2, 6 (col5)=A3, 7 (row6)=A4, 8 (row3)=A5, 9 (row1)=2, 10 (col4)=3, 11 (col6)=4, 12 (row4)=5, 13 (col1)=6, 14 (row2)=7, 15 (col7)=8, 16 (col8)=9.",
  "The 8 x 1k resistors sit on the yellow wires on Arduino pins 2-9, as in the image: resistor leg 1 in the Uno header socket, leg 2 joined to a yellow jumper that goes to the matrix pin. Pins 10-13 and A2-A5 go straight to the matrix by green jumpers.",
  "Breadboard rows in the image (1-30) are mapped to the catalogue's column numbers. Pot1 (rows 8-10) wiper goes to A1; pot2 (rows 13-15) wiper goes to A0. Pot GND/5V legs are wired to the right-hand rails; exact rail hole numbers are assumed because a rail is one strip.",
  "The Uno red/black wires go from 5V and GND.1 to the + and - rails. The tutorial does not say which GND header pin is used, so GND.1 was assumed.",
  "The Claude.ai Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors need authorization (via the claude.ai connector settings) before they can be used. They were not needed for this task."
 ],
